In .NET 10 MAUI, `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was removed because Android itself deprecated the `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` flag (API 30+). The modern replacement is the **WindowInsets** API.

## Quick Fix — `adjustResize` in the manifest

If you just need basic behavior, ensure your `Platforms/Android/AndroidManifest.xml` has:

```xml
<activity ... android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize" />
```

This still works at the manifest level for most layouts.

## Proper Fix — WindowInsets listener

For full control (especially edge-to-edge), add a platform-specific handler in `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Compatibility.Platform.Android;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new KeyboardInsetsListener());
}

class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBars = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        // Apply bottom padding = max(keyboard, nav bar)
        v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBars.Bottom));

        return insets;
    }
}
```

## Layout tip

Wrap your chat page in a `Grid` with the input bar at the bottom — **not** inside a `ScrollView`. The insets-based padding will push the entire layout up when the keyboard appears.

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <Entry Grid.Row="1" Placeholder="Type a message..." />
</Grid>
```

The key takeaway: replace the old enum-based resize mode with a `WindowInsetsCompat` listener that adjusts padding dynamically.
